123	
124	\begin{proof}
125	  \uses{lem:curve_hypothesis_gap, lem:pic0_relative_dimension_genus,
126	    lem:pic0_isAlbanese_all_points}
127	  Representability of the relative Picard functor gives \(\Pic_{C/k}\), and its
128	  identity component \(\Pic^0_{C/k}\) is a group scheme, smooth, proper and
129	  geometrically irreducible by \cref{thm:pic0_isAbelianVariety}. Those four data
130	  are the first four fields of the witness; of the four,
131	  \cref{thm:pic0_smooth} and \cref{thm:pic0_proper} are the ones whose own proofs
132	  are still open.
133	
134	  Three further steps are needed, and each is isolated as a lemma because it does
135	  not follow from the four above.
136	
137	  First, the hypotheses must be reconciled: \(\Pic^0_{C/k}\) is constructed for a
138	  geometrically \emph{integral} curve carrying a \(k\)-rational point, whereas a
139	  witness is required for every smooth proper geometrically irreducible curve.
140	  This is \cref{lem:curve_hypothesis_gap}.
141	
142	  Second, the smoothness supplied by \cref{thm:pic0_isAbelianVariety} carries no
143	  relative dimension, while the witness records smoothness at the specific
144	  relative dimension \(g(C)\); the tangent-space identification
145	  \(T_0\Pic^0_{C/k}\cong H^1(C,\mathcal O_C)\) of
146	  \cref{thm:pic_zero_dimension_equals_genus} supplies the dimension, and
147	  \cref{lem:pic0_relative_dimension_genus} is the resulting refinement.
148	
149	  Third, the Albanese structure is required for \emph{every} \(P\in C(k)\) and for
150	  every genus, whereas \cref{thm:albanese_universal_property_northstar} is proved
151	  over an algebraically closed base field and for \(g(C) > 0\); the extension is
152	  \cref{lem:pic0_isAlbanese_all_points}. Together these seven data form the
153	  required witness.
154	\end{proof}
